# Aston Martin DB11 V8 coupe, 2016-2023.
#
# The DB11: the first car of the second-century Aston range, with the long
# clamshell bonnet, the wide grille, the floating roof and the pronounced
# rear haunches. The V8 coupe the pack photographs is modelled; the V12 and
# the Volante are different variants or bodies.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aston_Martin_DB11
#
# Dimensions 4.750 x 1.948 x 1.290 m, wheelbase 2.804 m.
#
# Shape reference: a silver DB11 V8 coupe with a black roof panel in true
# side elevation, front three-quarter and rear three-quarter, all one car.
#
# Colours: grade (c), documented period cars. Silver, black, blue and British
# Racing Green are the plain names used. Weights 3, 3, 2, 2, total 10,
# provisional.
#
# Speed 301 km/h. Comfort 90/315, on the line 180 + 1.5 x 90. Classes 3,4.
# Dates are road presence: 2016 intro, retires staggered 2042-2045.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/aston-db11.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/aston-db11.dae. References:
# citycars/references/aston-db11/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the dark pillar area reads too broad, the wing vent is
# too small, and the two thin rear lamp blades and the diffuser are
# simplified. At 128 px the long bonnet, slatted grille and floating roof
# read as a DB11.


